-- title:
--   Error of the computed chirp transform
-- statement:
--   **Error of the computed chirp transform.** If `M̃C` is within `Ec·hp` of the bilinear contraction `MC` with output norm `≤ 1` (grid inputs, first of norm `≤ 1`, second `≤ 7/10`), and `ã` is a grid approximation of the unit phases `a`, then for `‖x‖ ≤ 6/10`: `‖C̃(x) - a · MC(a, a · x)‖ ≤ (Ec + 10)hp` and `‖C̃(x)‖ ≤ 1`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFMErr`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFM.chirp_err (p : ℕ) {MC MCt : (ι → ℂ) → (ι → ℂ) → (ι → ℂ)} (hMC : BilC MC) (Ec : ℝ)
--       (hMCt : ∀ f g, Grid p f → Grid p g → ‖f‖ ≤ 1 → ‖g‖ ≤ 7 / 10 →
--         ‖MCt f g - MC f g‖ ≤ Ec * hp p ∧ ‖MCt f g‖ ≤ 1)
--       {a at' b bt : ι → ℂ} (ha : Phases p a at') (hb' : Phases p b bt) (hbg : Grid p bt)
--       {x : ι → ℂ} (hx : ‖x‖ ≤ 6 / 10) :
--       ‖chirpT p MCt bt at' x - a * MC b (a * x)‖ ≤ (Ec + 10) * hp p ∧
--         ‖chirpT p MCt bt at' x‖ ≤ 1
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFM 14: the error chain of the computed pipeline (§9.7.1), abstract form*: Arrays are functions `ι → ℂ` with the sup norm; `hp = 2^{-p}`. Every computed procedure is
--   an arbitrary function with an error bound on grid inputs (`Grid p f`: `Q_p f = f`), so the IL
--   denotations (and `P18IL`) plug in later.
